## What this predicate means

**A `cites` B** — A references B as an external pointer.  The general-purpose citation typed-edge: a pattern cites a reference, a plan cites a library, a memoir cites a source consulted.  Stronger than `touches` (which is topical engagement without source-dependence); weaker than `evidences` (which asserts B BACKS a specific claim made in A).

